function.description:
Retrieve monitoring data for hosts based on specified filters. By default, if no filters are provided (empty object {}), all host data will be returned. Add parameters to filter and restrict the results. Examples:
- Get all hosts with alerts: {'alert_flag': true}
- Get latest data for specific host: {'dataset_id': 0, 'address': 'test.com'}
- Get historical data by time rangeand host id: {'id': 2, 'date_start': '2024-04-11T19:20:00', 'date_end': '2024-04-12T19:20:00'}
- Paginate through all hosts. Starting at page 1 with 10 hosts on it: {'page_number': 1, 'page_size': 10}

Note: Multiple filters can be combined (AND logic).IMPORTANT: ONLY SET FIELDS THAT YOU ARE FILTERING WITH. For example if you want the latest host data for host with a given address you only need to set the address and dataset_id all other fields are NOT needed.

Retrieve a list of monitored hosts and their configurations based on specified filters. By default, if no filters are provided (empty object {}), all hosts will be returned. Add parameters to filter and restrict the results. Examples:
- Get all hosts with '.com' addresses: {'address': '.com'}
- Get only DNS endpoint hosts: {'endpoint': 'dns'}
- Get enabled hosts from specific location: {'enabled': true, 'agent_location': 'London - UK'}
- Paginate through all hosts, show page 1 with 10 hosts on it: {'page_number': 1, 'page_size': 10}

Note: Multiple filters can be combined (AND logic). Leaving a filter out means that field won't be used to restrict results.IMPORTANT: ONLY SET FIELDS THAT YOU ARE FILTERING WITH. For example if you want the latest host config for host with a given address you only need to set the address all other fields are NOT needed.
